From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: fix AHB TX completion IRQ selection

The TX ring masks contain logical TCL ring indices.  The AHB IRQ setup
instead compares these masks against the mapped hardware WBM ring number.

This happens to work for the first three QCN9274 rings, whose logical TCL
and WBM ring numbers are identical.  The fourth logical ring maps to WBM
ring 4, however, so BIT(3) is compared against BIT(4) and its completion
IRQ is never requested.  Frames submitted through that ring consequently
remain pending and keep their TX descriptors and skbs allocated.

Match the TX mask using the logical ring index, as also expected by the
datapath service routine.  The IRQ resource remains selected by logical
ring index, so the fourth ring now uses the
wbm2host-tx-completions-ring4 resource.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -583,9 +583,11 @@ static int ath12k_ahb_config_ext_irq(str
 		netif_napi_add(irq_grp->napi_ndev, &irq_grp->napi,
 			       ath12k_ahb_ext_grp_napi_poll);
 
+		/* TX masks use logical TCL ring indices.  WBM ring numbers are
+		 * hardware mappings and are not necessarily contiguous.
+		 */
 		for (j = 0; j < DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX; j++) {
-			if (ring_mask->tx[i] &
-			    BIT(ab->hal.tcl_to_wbm_rbm_map[j].wbm_ring_num) &&
+			if (ring_mask->tx[i] & BIT(j) &&
 			    num_irq < ATH12K_EXT_IRQ_NUM_MAX) {
 				irq_grp->irqs[num_irq++] =
 					wbm2host_tx_completions_ring1 - j;
